  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nDry conditions with above normal temperatures \npersist through the weekend. This will exacerbate ongoing water\nresource drought conditions.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nDeep layered ridging continues to build in tonight and Wednesday\nwith associated subsidence keeping things dry. At the surface, \nhigh pressure builds in to the southwest through midweek. Another\nweak upper level trough slides across the region Friday. However,\nthe lingering surface high will contain any chance of precipitation\nthrough the weekend.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nThere may be a brief chance for some precipitation early next \nweek before high pressure returns. Any drought relief is \nunlikely.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\nErn trof will be digging into the northeast as a coastal low moves \nup the eastern seaboard late weekend or early next week. 12Z \noperational GFS is quicker and further west with s/wv in sw flow \naloft which results in coastal low passing closer to Downeast with \nhigher qpf totals impacting the area. 12z EC AI is similar to GFS \nwith a track closer to the coast. Ensembles are still all over the \nplace with the track of the system in relation to the cold front. \nDepending on how these two interact with each other will determine \nwhat location sees higher rainfall totals, if any.\n\nOne thing all of the ensembles agree on is that cold and dry weather \nwill move in on Canadian high pressure following fropa.",
